#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:6
msgid "Publishing messages using YAML files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:8
msgid "**Goal:** Record and replay topics using YAML files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:10
msgid "**Tutorial level:** Intermediate"
msgstr "**教學等級：** 中級"

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:12
msgid "**Time:** 5 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:16
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr "目次表"

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:19
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "概覽"

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:21
msgid ""
"Publishing ROS 2 messages via CLI is straightforward for simple types like "
"`std_msgs/msg/Bool <https://docs.ros.org/en/rolling/p/std_msgs/msg/Bool."
"html>`_ or `std_msgs/msg/String <https://docs.ros.org/en/rolling/p/std_msgs/"
"msg/String.html>`_. However, it becomes tedious for complex message "
"structures. This tutorial demonstrates how to use ``ros2 echo`` and ``ros2 "
"pub`` with YAML files to record, edit, and replay topic data efficiently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:26
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr "先備條件"

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:28
msgid ""
"This tutorial uses concepts like ROS 2 topics and CLI tools covered in the "
"following tutorial:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:30
msgid ""
":doc:`Understanding topics <../../ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/"
"Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:33
msgid "Tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:35
msgid ""
"We assume that an entity is publishing a `geometry_msgs/msg/Twist <https://"
"docs.ros.org/en/rolling/p/geometry_msgs/msg/Twist.html>`_ message through a "
"topic named ``cmd_vel`` and we want to capture the message, edit it and "
"publish it to a topic. We can use the ``echo`` verb to capture the message "
"and save it in a YAML file ``cmd_vel.yaml`` using the output redirection "
"operator ``>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:38
msgid "$ ros2 topic echo --once  /cmd_vel > cmd_vel.yaml"
msgstr "$ ros2 topic echo --once  /cmd_vel > cmd_vel.yaml"

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:42
msgid ""
"This creates a ``cmd_vel.yaml`` file with the following content in the "
"directory the command was executed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:44
msgid ""
"linear:\n"
"    x: 1.0\n"
"    y: 0.0\n"
"    z: 0.0\n"
"angular:\n"
"    x: 0.0\n"
"    y: 0.0\n"
"    z: 0.0\n"
"---"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:56
msgid ""
"To publish a message, we utilize the ``--yaml-file`` option available with "
"the ``pub`` verb of the ``ros2 topic`` command. First, we specify the target "
"topic—in this case, ``/cmd_vel``, followed by the message type "
"`geometry_msgs/msg/Twist <https://docs.ros.org/en/rolling/p/geometry_msgs/"
"msg/Twist.html>`_. Lastly, we specify the YAML file containing the message "
"data. The following command will publish the message contained in the "
"``YAML`` file to the designated ``topic`` once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:61
msgid ""
"$ ros2 topic pub /cmd_vel geometry_msgs/msg/Twist --yaml-file cmd_vel.yaml\n"
"publisher: beginning loop\n"
"publishing geometry_msgs.msg.Twist(linear=geometry_msgs.msg.Vector3(x=1.0, "
"y=0.0, z=0.0), angular=geometry_msgs.msg.Vector3(x=0.0, y=0.0, z=0.0))"
msgstr ""
"$ ros2 topic pub /cmd_vel geometry_msgs/msg/Twist --yaml-file cmd_vel.yaml\n"
"publisher: beginning loop\n"
"publishing geometry_msgs.msg.Twist(linear=geometry_msgs.msg.Vector3(x=1.0, "
"y=0.0, z=0.0), angular=geometry_msgs.msg.Vector3(x=0.0, y=0.0, z=0.0))"

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:67
msgid ""
"You can also publish more than once by adding more data to the YAML file as "
"demonstrated in the example below. In this case two messages where added to "
"the YAML file with different values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:70
msgid ""
"linear:\n"
"    x: 1.0\n"
"    y: 0.0\n"
"    z: 0.0\n"
"angular:\n"
"    x: 0.0\n"
"    y: 0.0\n"
"    z: 0.0\n"
"---\n"
"linear:\n"
"    x: 2.0\n"
"    y: 0.0\n"
"    z: 0.0\n"
"angular:\n"
"    x: 0.0\n"
"    y: 0.0\n"
"    z: 0.0\n"
"---\n"
"linear:\n"
"    x: 3.0\n"
"    y: 0.0\n"
"    z: 0.0\n"
"angular:\n"
"    x: 0.0\n"
"    y: 0.0\n"
"    z: 0.0\n"
"---"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:100
msgid ""
"By executing the same command as before, we publish three different messages "
"to the ``/cmd_vel`` topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Publishing-Messages-Using-YAML-Files.rst:102
msgid ""
"$ ros2 topic pub /cmd_vel geometry_msgs/msg/Twist --yaml-file cmd_vel.yaml\n"
"publisher: beginning loop\n"
"publishing #1: geometry_msgs.msg.Twist(linear=geometry_msgs.msg."
"Vector3(x=1.0, y=0.0, z=0.0), angular=geometry_msgs.msg.Vector3(x=0.0, "
"y=0.0, z=0.0))\n"
"\n"
"publishing #2: geometry_msgs.msg.Twist(linear=geometry_msgs.msg."
"Vector3(x=3.0, y=0.0, z=0.0), angular=geometry_msgs.msg.Vector3(x=0.0, "
"y=0.0, z=0.0))\n"
"\n"
"publishing #3: geometry_msgs.msg.Twist(linear=geometry_msgs.msg."
"Vector3(x=2.0, y=0.0, z=0.0), angular=geometry_msgs.msg.Vector3(x=0.0, "
"y=0.0, z=0.0))"
msgstr ""
"$ ros2 topic pub /cmd_vel geometry_msgs/msg/Twist --yaml-file cmd_vel.yaml\n"
"publisher: beginning loop\n"
"publishing #1: geometry_msgs.msg.Twist(linear=geometry_msgs.msg."
"Vector3(x=1.0, y=0.0, z=0.0), angular=geometry_msgs.msg.Vector3(x=0.0, "
"y=0.0, z=0.0))\n"
"\n"
"publishing #2: geometry_msgs.msg.Twist(linear=geometry_msgs.msg."
"Vector3(x=3.0, y=0.0, z=0.0), angular=geometry_msgs.msg.Vector3(x=0.0, "
"y=0.0, z=0.0))\n"
"\n"
"publishing #3: geometry_msgs.msg.Twist(linear=geometry_msgs.msg."
"Vector3(x=2.0, y=0.0, z=0.0), angular=geometry_msgs.msg.Vector3(x=0.0, "
"y=0.0, z=0.0))"

